# ApplyEasy — environment template
#
# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in GROQ_API_KEY.
#
#     cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#
# The path matters: backend/src/api/main.py hard-pins load_dotenv() to
# backend/.env rather than searching upward, so a .env at the repo root is
# ignored. Both .env and *.env are gitignored, so your real file stays local.
#
# Note that OUTPUT_DIR and DB_PATH are read at module import time. main.py
# calls load_dotenv() before importing anything under backend.src, which is why
# its import block is ordered the way it is - do not "tidy" those imports above
# the load_dotenv() call or these two stop taking effect.
#
# pytest does not load this file (there is no conftest.py). Tests mock every LLM
# call, so they need no key.


# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Groq API key - the LLM provider for every generation call.
# Get one at https://console.groq.com. The app is Groq-only; ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# is referenced nowhere in the codebase despite older doc claims.
# Without this, /generate accepts the request and the background run fails.
GROQ_API_KEY=


# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SQLite database file. Relative paths resolve against the working directory,
# which must be the repo root (see README).
# DB_PATH=resume_tool.db

# Directory for generated PDFs and change_summary.json, one subdirectory per
# run_id. Contains user PII - it is gitignored at the repo root as /outputs/.
# OUTPUT_DIR=outputs


# ── Planned - NOT READ BY THE CODE YET ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Listed so you know what is coming, not so you can set it today. Nothing below
# has any effect until the roadmap item named against it lands; setting these
# now does nothing at all. This block gets promoted above as each one is wired.
#
# Pipeline tier defaults and per-stage model selection (ROADMAP B1/B4):
# APPLYEASY_DEFAULT_TIER=standard          # standard | pro
# APPLYEASY_EXTRACTION_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant
# APPLYEASY_JD_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant
# APPLYEASY_REWRITE_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
#
# Repair loop (ROADMAP B5):
# APPLYEASY_REPAIR_PASSES=1                # 0 disables; Pro default 1
#
# Run-level safety (ROADMAP D3):
# APPLYEASY_PIPELINE_DEADLINE_SECONDS=120
#
# Deployment (ROADMAP D7) - CORS origins are hardcoded to localhost today:
# APPLYEASY_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://app.example.com
